  "body": "## Summary\n\n- Build Linux x86_64 binaries on Ubuntu 22.04 and package them as TAR.GZ, DEB, and RPM.\n- Download those packages into the existing Windows release job, which publishes all five assets after both jobs succeed.\n- Add Linux installation instructions to the README.\n\nThe DEB and RPM keep binaries beside their assets under `/usr/lib/camcraft` and provide command-line launchers plus a desktop entry. The portable TAR.GZ keeps the same adjacent-asset layout as the Windows ZIP.\n\n## Verification\n\n- On Fedora 44, `cargo build --locked --release -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post` succeeded.\n- `scripts/package-linux.sh` produced a 28 MB TAR.GZ, 19 MB DEB, and 20 MB RPM for version 0.12.1; package metadata and portable archive contents were inspected.\n- Shell syntax, workflow YAML parsing, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- The GitHub hosted Ubuntu job has not been run yet. It can be tested with a manual `workflow_dispatch` on this branch before merge.\n\nThis is the first Linux slice of #72. AUR, FreeBSD, and Web/WASM remain open for separate work.\n\nChangelog: Add Linux x86_64 TAR.GZ, DEB, and RPM assets to tagged releases.\n\nRefs #72\n",
